{"name":"Bambino","hex":"#8edacc","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bambino","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A child or baby, especially a representation in art of the infant Christ wrapped in swaddling clothes. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bambino"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bambino (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bambino\" is a song recorded by Italian-French singer Dalida that became her first major hit. It was first released on 28 October 1956 as the title song of her third EP, prior to her debut album Son nom est Dalida, where it was also included. It is a French version of the Neapolitan song \"Guaglione\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c9/Bambino_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bambino_(song)","wikidata":"Q2745450"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c9/Bambino_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg/250px-Bambino_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c9/Bambino_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c9/Bambino_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg/250px-Bambino_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABambino_EP_by_recording_artist_Dalida.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/Bambino_EP_Dalida.jpeg/250px-Bambino_EP_Dalida.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Bambino_EP_Dalida.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign